Z||000000||WampusCat||12-02-2000||06:08 PM||||Hi everyone,  I've been lurking here for a while while I'm looking for my 1st Fiero.  I thought I had found the perfect car this week.  88 GT with sunroof and 58000 mi for $2800.  This sounded a little too good to be true so I ran a Carfax report and it turns out it was issued a salvage title in '99 and a reconstructed title in '00.  I drove the car and it seems fine but when I asked why it had been painted, the guy said it had been in a "fender bender."  Should I run away from this car or is there a chance it could be a good deal?  Thanks for and advice.||||reg||5
Z||000001||ur2biteme||12-02-2000||07:09 PM||||if i were you, i'd confront him with the carfax report and see how low he'll go on the price.  that's just me.  look real close on the car for things that seem out of place, like what seem like fresh welds or anything like that.  check for leaks, irregularly worn tires, odd sounds while driving, a pulling to any side, etc.  you may have allready known that though.  but i wouldnt exactly give up on the car just yet.  remember how low these cars book for and how high the cost of repairs is.  knowing how much body shops charge, some minor to moderate damage could total a fiero, but not come close to that on a newer car (even like a hyundai accent &lt;vommit&gt; ).  the car may still in fact be good, i'd just be doing some thinking and discussing with the owner of the car now, and make a well though decision, unless something better comes along<P>------------------<BR>UR2BITEME<BR>'87 econo coupe<BR>170k and a bad fender :(||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||12-02-2000||07:21 PM||||  Wampus, there are a few things you may not understand about Fiero's. That car could very well have been in just a fender bender. The fact that GM has discontinued so may of the parts makes them unrepairable from an insurance standpoint. I just went through this with my 85GT. The cost of the repairs as I made them were about $200.00. The fact that the repair facility could not locate "NEW" replacement parts (quarter panel, sail panel, rocker and door skin) it was deemed a total loss. I went to a wrecking yard and got all the parts I needed or purchased them off the Forum or E-Bay for under $200.00. All the problems solved. Now the insurance company wanted to settle with me and was going to list it as a total loss. I took a lesser settlement and it's not listed as such. Generaly, the fact that parts are no longer "available" will lead to this situation. Look at the car real good. Tell the seller that there is a carfax report as you mentioned, then offer him a little less. Bang, You've got yourself an awesome deal. Just my 2 cents.<P>  Peace, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||12
Z||000003||WampusCat||12-02-2000||07:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ur2biteme:<BR><B>look real close on the car for things that seem out of place, like...irregularly worn tires, <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Hmm...I didn't think much of it at the time, but it's got 2 brand new front tires while the backs have medium tread wear.  I guess there could be a logical reason for this other than bent frame but something else to think about.  Guess I'll just ask a lot of questions and ask for the name of mech that did the repairs.  I guess it'd be worth paying for a mech to check out this one.<P>Nervous Steve J. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||ur2biteme||12-03-2000||02:26 AM||||bam-bam.....<P>never thought about the body parts not being made anymore.  good thing i own my car, it's in a "totaled" condition right now.  lol.||||reg||1
Z||000005||WampusCat||12-04-2000||08:38 PM||||Well, I took the plunge and bought the car today.  I've been crawling under and all over it this afternoon and can't find anything bent or rusty.  It has a front facia from a coupe but I kinda like the combo.  All the power stuff inside works and the tan cloth seats with pwr.lumbar are in good shape.  Things I've found bad so far:  tach is erratic, seller had installed mini-tach on dash - ordered filter from Rodney Dickman's web site.  Left headlight "slips" during extension - found bushings crumbled, ordered new ones.  Springs on "trunk lid" on rear disconnected - looks hard to fix, using stick to prop open.  Driver's seat doesn't move - luckily it's where it needs to be for me, project for tommorrow.  Thing is a hoot to drive!  Engine is stock other than K&N and engine chip from Hypertech here in Memphis.  Woohoo!||||reg||1
